# Local-first emulation (mandatory)

The app runs **only on device / local storage**. There is no backend. Features are emulated: session, KYC, balances, funding, card, inbox.

**Data:** Local data sources and an in-app ledger only. Repositories must not call production payment, KYC, or bank APIs. Seed fixtures for screens. Flavor config may add a remote **later**; features stay against repository ports so the swap is Data-only.

**Settlement still applies.** Fake submits use `requestId` and `inFlight` → `confirmed` / `failed` / `unknown` (delay or local worker). Do not treat a local write as instantly settled if the product would wait.

**Prices / trading:** Until a remote price feed exists, quotes are cached fixtures with freshness `stale` or `disconnected`. Do not mark fixture prices `live`. Swap, buy, and any quote-sized submit stay rejected until a live remote (or explicit `dev` simulator) quote exists. Then follow Market data: `live` required to submit.

```text
❌ BAD — call a real card processor or mark a hardcoded BTC price as live
✅ GOOD — local ledger emulates Add funds; trade submits wait for a live remote quote
```
